CHAIN REMOVAL -- does the radar processing carry any maneuver information?
  LAG_MODE=lag  ACTUATOR_LAG_S=1.2  RESAMPLE=causal  aspect=0.80  cue SNR +20 dB
  full   = cue -> micro_doppler -> spectrogram -> band power -> matched-FPR threshold
  direct = cue ----------------------------------------------> matched-FPR threshold

quantity                              value
--------------------------------------------
paired tracks                            30
median lead, full chain              +0.400 s
median lead, chain removed           +0.200 s
PAIRED median difference             +0.000 s
tracks bit-identical                    83 %
difference of medians (unpaired)     +0.200 s
max |paired difference|              +5.000 s
Wilcoxon (two-sided) p                0.121

READING: a paired median of 0.000 s with most tracks bit-identical means the entire
  spectrogram-and-band-power chain is invertible with respect to the decision -- it
  carries no information the threshold on the cue did not already have. The unpaired
  difference of medians is a DIFFERENT quantity and is not the claim.
